<task id="023" project="spaarkeai-compose-r6">
  <metadata>
    <title>Headers/footers + page breaks through the canonical model</title>
    <phase>2 Canonical model + fidelity widening</phase>
    <gate>dep:020</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <completion-note>COMPLETED 2026-08-06 (commits 5951f173b + b9f15df02, pushed). Executed at FULL rigor
      (Step 0.5 override UP from authored STANDARD — modifies .cs on the BFF hot-path, bff-api tags;
      adr-check confirmed the escalation as the correct protocol reading). Two mechanisms: (1)
      HEADERS/FOOTERS ride the CARRIER — parts preserved byte-identically by RenderIntoCarrier and the
      trailing sectPr's headerReference/footerReference PROVEN to resolve post-round-trip (per-doc +
      corpus-wide theory); editing header content is not an editor capability and template part-merge is
      Phase 3. (2) PAGE BREAKS are MODEL data — the real gap (a manual w:br type=page degraded to a SPACE
      before this task): ComposeInlineRun.IsPageBreak captured at the EXACT inline position (ProjectRun
      flush-split) + ComposeBlock.PageBreakBefore (OnOff), both re-authored (BuildRun break-run;
      ApplyPageBreakBefore in CT_PPr order across all three builders). Interior section breaks flatten
      LOUDLY via the new counted section-break-flattened warning — EXCEPT the 011-P1 promotion shape,
      which the renderer promotes losslessly and therefore must not warn (Step-9.5 F1). Soft line/column
      breaks remain warned flattens. SEAM: ComposeHeaderFooterPageBreakSeamTests (14) — exact-position
      capture, parts identity + reference resolution, break fixed point, interior-section loud flatten +
      no-hard-fail (landscape final section preserved), P-1 no-warn + promotion, corpus reference +
      break-count stability, multiset validator. Step 9.5: adr-check PASS 8/8; code-review
      APPROVE-WITH-MINORS → F1/F3/F4 fixed, F2 documented degradation (pageBreakBefore val=false
      collapse), F5-F8 recorded. Gates: suite 719/722 (3 pre-existing NDA-class reds); ADR-013 green;
      publish 46.89 MB incl PDBs clean-worktree (task delta 0.00); no package/DI/endpoint change.
      Record: notes/020-canonical-hub-design.md §13 + §13.1.</completion-note>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
