  <prompt>
    Route headers/footers + page breaks through the canonical document model (from task 020). Prove header/footer
    content and page breaks load → edit → save → reopen round-trip through the model without hard-fail, authored as
    Word-valid w:headerReference/w:footerReference (+ header/footer parts) and page-break markup on the
    render-on-save path.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in OOXML section properties and header/footer parts (w:sectPr, w:headerReference/w:footerReference, header/footer XML parts, w:br type="page" / w:lastRenderedPageBreak), and the Compose canonical model + render-on-save author. Follow ADRs strictly; keep Services/Compose byte[]-in / projection-out.</role>

  <goal>Headers/footers and page breaks flow through the canonical model: the projection captures header/footer content + page-break positions and the renderer authors valid w:headerReference/w:footerReference (with header/footer parts) and page-break markup on the render-on-save path. A seam slice proves each construct round-trips (load→edit→save→reopen) without hard-fail.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-04: headers/footers and page breaks are near-term fidelity features that must round-trip through the canonical model without hard-fail. ComposeDocumentRenderer.AppendSection (:142) already handles section-level authoring, giving a render precedent to follow. (Note: template chrome part-merge for firm/matter .dotx is Phase 3 — this task is the model's own header/footer/page-break round-trip only.)</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Compose/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">The generalized canonical document model (the single hub headers/footers/page breaks flow through).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Save renders headers/footers/page breaks from the canonical model per the Path-B amendment — NO surgical byte-patch, NO text-search on the save path.</constraint>
