  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a corpus doc with headers/footers and page breaks, when it loads → edit → save → reopen, then they round-trip through the canonical model without hard-fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a save, then header/footer references (+ parts) and page-break markup are authored from the canonical model on the render-on-save path with no surgical byte-patch and no text-search.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative / no-regression: Tier-1 NetArchTest passes; docxBridge.ts not deleted; BFF publish ≤60 MB with delta reported vs ~49.63 MB; seam slice uses no banned mock/DI/ctor shapes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-04; plan.md §5 Phase 2. Template-chrome part-merge is Phase 3, not here. Builds on 020; seam-tested with the rest in 027. parallel-safe=false. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</notes>

